<title>USA: ComEd 1,105 MW Byron 2 nuclear unit shuts.</title>
<headline>ComEd 1,105 MW Byron 2 nuclear unit shuts.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Edison Co's 1,105 megawatt (MW) Byron 2 nuclear unit shut down Saturday for maintenance, the Nuclear Regulatory Commission (NRC) said Monday in its plant status report.</p>
<p>The unit, which was operating in hot shutdown mode, is expected to restart this Wednesday, the NRC report stated.</p>
<p>No further details were given in the report.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit 1, with an identical generating capacity, was operating at full power. Both units are located in Byron, Ill.</p>
<p>ComEd is a subsidiary of Unicom Corp.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
